A||||2||Eric||Good Race?||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||08-26-2001||03:22 PM||||I had a little street race with a newer Eclipse FWD turbo car yesterday.  The guy was hotrodding the little rice dryer all around the road behind me, so I had to give him some attention.  I stopped short at the next yellow and he lined up next to me in the left lane.  After seeing the giant rear wing and 16" factory wheels, I was pretty sure it was a turbo.  Once we were both stopped at the yellow, I asked him if his car was a turbo.  He said yeah, so I told him mine was only a little six.  After assuring him he would walk all over me, I asked if he want to go a little bit from the light.  He gave me the nod.  <P>I decided I'd just go from an idle, not trying to launch hard and potentially break loose.  He pinned the throttle and dropped the clutch, spinning his tires when the light turned.  I bogged down (I'm used to racing the cobra which will spin the tires like mad with even the most gentle of throttle application).  So with our equally poor launches, we were pretty much even through 50mph, me holding a slight advantage.  Of course, once that turbo started doing its job, there was little hope for my dinky little Fiero.  He had about a car length on me at 70mph when he shut it down and gave me a wave.  <P>Hell, I knew I would loose, so it didn't upset me much.  The dude's girlfriend was probably pretty impressed with him, bonus for the riceboy.  And the race was a good, clean respectful one.  So everyone came away feelin' pretty good.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cheever3000||08-26-2001||03:28 PM||||Yep.  Good race.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||08-26-2001||05:53 PM||||Raced a 5.0 mustang today from a rolling start. We were both lined up at the light. I started to take off from the light normally and he was gassing it more than I was. At about 10 mph he had a half car on me so I decided that I was going to punch it and see how I would fare. I reeled him in pretty quickly even though I shifted @ 5000 rpm and by the time I got to 60 mph I had 3/4 car length on him. I would have kept gaining ground on him but the speed got to high and there was traffic up ahead so I slowed down. He gave me the thumbs up and I did too.  <P>He had an exhaust system and from what I could tell he also had a manual transmission.<P>Any ideas on what a car like that can run in the quarter?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
